1. What does the `.map()` array method do?
    Iterates over each item in an array, performing a function on each.
    Returns a new array with modified values in the same indexes.


2. What do we usually use `.map()` for in React?
    Convert arrays of raw data into arrays of JSX elements to be displayed on the page.


3. Critical thinking: why is using `.map()` better than just
   creating the components manually by typing them out?
    Reusability. Hard coding things is generally only good for very small scale projects, or items that will not be changed.